# Firebase Configuration (already configured)
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-api-key
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your-sender-id
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your-app-id

# YouTube Data API v3 Configuration (Required for Create page)
VITE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.googleusercontent.com
VITE_YOUTUBE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-oauth-client-secret
VITE_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your-youtube-data-api-key

# Instructions:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console (https://console.cloud.google.com/)
# 2. Create a new project or select existing one
# 3. Enable YouTube Data API v3
# 4. Create OAuth 2.0 credentials:
#    - Application type: Web application
#    - Authorized origins: http://localhost:8080, https://your-domain.com
#    - Authorized redirect URIs: http://localhost:8080/auth/youtube/callback.html, https://your-domain.com/auth/youtube/callback.html
# 5. Create API Key for YouTube Data API v3
# 6. Copy the credentials to your .env.local file